---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="External Parquet ingest — Querial">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-querial-indigo-on-dark">For Developers</p>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mt-1">External Parquet ingest</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 [&>p]:text-muted-foreground [&>h2]:text-foreground [&>h3]:text-foreground">
            <p>
                Some pipelines should start from a Parquet file the caller already has —
                a nightly drop, a partner extract, a test fixture — not from a database
                query. The <code class="text-foreground">external-parquet</code> step is
                that root. It produces a Parquet artifact. It has no SQL body and no
                logical connection. Downstream Artifact SQL or Staged Database SQL bind
                with <code class="text-foreground">from_step</code> the same way they
                bind an extract.
            </p>

            <h2>What the step is</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li>A <strong class="text-foreground">structural root</strong>: publish requires indegree 0. You cannot hang it under another step.</li>
                <li>A Parquet <strong class="text-foreground">producer</strong>. It does not consume artifacts.</li>
                <li>Required unique <code class="text-foreground">outputName</code> (no file extension) among producers in the pipeline.</li>
                <li>Optional <code class="text-foreground">expectedSchema</code> — a fingerprint / column contract. Mismatch fails <em>before</em> a run is created.</li>
                <li>Optional <code class="text-foreground">retentionDays</code> (1–3650). Omit uses the artifact store default (30). Expired objects cannot be reused on a failed-cone.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Multiple ingest roots are allowed (a forest), same as multiple extracts.
                Each <code class="text-foreground">outputName</code> needs its own file
                at trigger time. Extra files are rejected.
            </p>

            <h2>How a run is seeded</h2>
            <p>
                The file is not fetched by an agent. The control plane validates the
                upload (size, Parquet footer, optional schema), creates the run and DAG
                plan, writes the bytes into the artifact store, and marks those ingest
                executions <strong class="text-foreground">succeeded</strong> before
                readiness evaluation. Downstream <code class="text-foreground">from_step</code>
                still means <em>same run</em>. If an agent ever leases an ingest step
                that was not seeded, the handler fails closed — it does not invent an
                empty file.
            </p>
            <p>
                JSON-only trigger of a version that has ingest steps is rejected. Use
                multipart (API) or the Run now modal (Web). Limits default to 100 MiB
                per file and 256 MiB per request. Files are never JSON-base64.
            </p>

            <h2>Not schedulable</h2>
            <p>
                Cron cannot attach a file. Create and enable of a schedule targeting an
                ingest version are refused. If a leftover schedule fires anyway, the run
                is inserted as Failed with a stable message — no empty artifact. Use
                <a href="/docs/devops-trigger" class="text-link hover:underline">API trigger</a>
                or Web Run now.
            </p>

            <h2>Package shape</h2>
            <p>
                Additive on <code class="text-foreground">querial.package/v1</code>. No
                <code class="text-foreground">connection:</code>, no <code class="text-foreground">sql:</code>
                file. Runtime identities (<code class="text-foreground">artifactId</code>,
                store URI, checksum) are forbidden in the tree.
            </p>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>steps:
  - code: ingest_ids
    name: Upload ids Parquet
    type: external-parquet
    execution_order: 10
    config:
      outputName: ids
      retentionDays: 30
  - code: load_ids
    name: Load ids
    type: staged-database-sql
    execution_order: 20
    connection: ingest-pg-dest
    sql: sql/steps/020_load_ids.sql
    config:
      stages:
        ids:
          from_step: ingest_ids
          columns:
            - source: id
              name: id
              type: int
              nullable: false

dependencies:
  - from: ingest_ids
    to: load_ids
    requirement: artifact_available</code></pre>
            <p>
                Sink SQL uses <code class="text-foreground">{"{{ stage.ids }}"}</code>,
                never a physical staging name. A ready-made lab package (fixture
                <code class="text-foreground">tiny-ids.parquet</code>) follows this
                shape — import is an operator action; this role reviews the draft DAG
                and publishes.
            </p>

            <h2>Retry and failed-cone</h2>
            <p>
                Seeded ingest artifacts default <em>safe</em> for auto-retry (same as
                extract / Artifact SQL). Failed-cone recovery <strong class="text-foreground">reuses</strong>
                live ingest objects (same store URI and expiry). If the object is gone
                or expired, cone is refused — the operator must full-retry
                <em>with files</em>. Re-executing an ingest node always requires a new
                upload. See
                <a href="/docs/developer-retry" class="text-link hover:underline">Step retry policies</a>
                and
                <a href="/docs/devops-retry" class="text-link hover:underline">Retry and failed-cone recovery</a>.
            </p>

            <h2>Designer notes</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li>The node has no SQL editor and no connection picker. Drop onto a connection group is invalid.</li>
                <li>Wait any is disabled on ingest (it is a data producer, not a control gate).</li>
                <li>Requires DAG execution and artifacts flags. Legacy serial execution must not run this type.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Trigger-time parameters still apply. Uploading a file does not skip
                parameter validation. Merge is trigger overlay, then deployment override,
                then pipeline default —
                <a href="/docs/devops-trigger" class="text-link hover:underline">Trigger API and Run now</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
